{
  "$comment": [
    "Shared cross-language corpus for the transcript turn assembler.",
    "",
    "Two implementations reconstruct conversation turns from the same event log:",
    "packages/mewbo_core/src/mewbo_core/transcript_timeline.py (canonical) and",
    "apps/mewbo_console/src/utils/timeline.ts (buildTimeline). Their own unit",
    "tests only ever checked each side against itself, so a rule added to one and",
    "missed by the other shipped silently \u2014 which is how the Python port came to",
    "render no plan, todos, widget, run_failure or question rows at all.",
    "",
    "This file is the contract between them. Each case is an event log plus the",
    "rows BOTH implementations must produce. `expected` was written from the",
    "documented rules, not dumped from either implementation: an expectation",
    "generated from the code under test only proves the code equals itself.",
    "",
    "Field spelling is the TS `TimelineEntry` shape (camelCase `turnId`); the",
    "Python side maps snake_case when it replays this file. `ts` is null wherever",
    "the assembler deliberately sets none (a `plan` row and an assistant closure",
    "both carry the turn's own timing instead).",
    "",
    "Adding a role to either implementation without adding a case here fails",
    "test_every_role_is_represented_in_the_corpus."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "single_turn",
      "why": "A user event opens a turn; the next assistant event closes it.",
      "events": [
        {
          "type": "user",
          "ts": "t0",
          "payload": {
            "text": "hi"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "assistant",
          "ts": "t9",
          "payload": {
            "text": "hello"
          }
        }
      ],
      "expected": [
        {
          "id": "user-1",
          "role": "user",
          "turnId": "turn-1",
          "content": "hi",
          "ts": "t0"
        },
        {
          "id": "assistant-1",
          "role": "assistant",
          "turnId": "turn-1",
          "content": "hello",
          "ts": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "completion_closes_an_unclosed_turn",
      "why": "Defensive fallback: a completion closes a turn no assistant event did.",
      "events": [
        {
          "type": "user",
          "ts": "t0",
          "payload": {
            "text": "go"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "completion",
          "ts": "t9",
          "payload": {
            "done_reason": "stop"
          }
        }
      ],
      "expected": [
        {
          "id": "user-1",
          "role": "user",
          "turnId": "turn-1",
          "content": "go",
          "ts": "t0"
        },
        {
          "id": "completion-1",
          "role": "assistant",
          "turnId": "turn-1",
          "content": "(run ended)",
          "ts": "t9"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "interrupted_turn_is_materialised",
      "why": "A turn the next prompt superseded keeps its body instead of vanishing. Its ts is the LAST body event, since no closure ever arrived.",
      "events": [
        {
          "type": "user",
          "ts": "t0",
          "payload": {
            "text": "one"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "tool_result",
          "ts": "t1",
          "payload": {
            "tool_id": "shell"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "user",
          "ts": "t2",
          "payload": {
            "text": "two"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "assistant",
          "ts": "t3",
          "payload": {
            "text": "done"
          }
        }
      ],
      "expected": [
        {
          "id": "user-1",
          "role": "user",
          "turnId": "turn-1",
          "content": "one",
          "ts": "t0"
        },
        {
          "id": "interrupted-1",
          "role": "run_failed",
          "turnId": "turn-1",
          "content": "",
          "ts": "t1"
        },
        {
          "id": "user-2",
          "role": "user",
          "turnId": "turn-2",
          "content": "two",
          "ts": "t2"
        },
        {
          "id": "assistant-2",
          "role": "assistant",
          "turnId": "turn-2",
          "content": "done",
          "ts": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "synthetic_closure_is_upgraded_in_place",
      "why": "The orchestrator's placeholder carries nothing the failure record lacks, so the failure replaces it and the row keeps its id.",
      "events": [
        {
          "type": "user",
          "ts": "t0",
          "payload": {
            "text": "go"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "assistant",
          "ts": "t8",
          "payload": {
            "text": "(Run stopped: upstream died)"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "completion",
          "ts": "t9",
          "payload": {
            "done_reason": "error",
            "error": "upstream died"
          }
        }
      ],
      "expected": [
        {
          "id": "user-1",
          "role": "user",
          "turnId": "turn-1",
          "content": "go",
          "ts": "t0"
        },
        {
          "id": "assistant-1",
          "role": "run_failed",
          "turnId": "turn-1",
          "content": "",
          "ts": "t9"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "failure_on_real_prose_keeps_the_answer",
      "why": "A boot sweep can append a completion to an orphaned run; the prose is the only copy of what it produced, so the failure lands beside it.",
      "events": [
        {
          "type": "user",
          "ts": "t0",
          "payload": {
            "text": "go"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "assistant",
          "ts": "t8",
          "payload": {
            "text": "Here is the real answer."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "completion",
          "ts": "t9",
          "payload": {
            "done_reason": "error",
            "error": "run died"
          }
        }
      ],
      "expected": [
        {
          "id": "user-1",
          "role": "user",
          "turnId": "turn-1",
          "content": "go",
          "ts": "t0"
        },
        {
          "id": "assistant-1",
          "role": "assistant",
          "turnId": "turn-1",
          "content": "Here is the real answer.",
          "ts": null
        },
        {
          "id": "run-failed-t9",
          "role": "run_failed",
          "turnId": "turn-1",
          "content": "",
          "ts": "t9"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "markers_between_turns_survive_the_gate",
      "why": "Trigger, recovery, compaction and termination all legitimately arrive with no turn open; gating them would discard every one.",
      "events": [
        {
          "type": "user",
          "ts": "t0",
          "payload": {
            "text": "q1"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "assistant",
          "ts": "t1",
          "payload": {
            "text": "a1"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "trigger_fired",
          "ts": "t2",
          "payload": {
            "trigger_id": "tr1",
            "kind": "time.at",
            "payload_summary": "woke"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "recovery",
          "ts": "t3",
          "payload": {
            "action": "continue"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "context_compacted",
          "ts": "t4",
          "payload": {
            "depth": 0,
            "mode": "auto",
            "tokens_saved": 4200
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "session_terminated",
          "ts": "t5",
          "payload": {}
        }
      ],
      "expected": [
        {
          "id": "user-1",
          "role": "user",
          "turnId": "turn-1",
          "content": "q1",
          "ts": "t0"
        },
        {
          "id": "assistant-1",
          "role": "assistant",
          "turnId": "turn-1",
          "content": "a1",
          "ts": null
        },
        {
          "id": "trigger-fired-t2",
          "role": "trigger",
          "turnId": "triggers",
          "content": "",
          "ts": "t2"
        },
        {
          "id": "recovery-t3",
          "role": "recovery",
          "turnId": "recovery",
          "content": "",
          "ts": "t3"
        },
        {
          "id": "compaction-t4",
          "role": "compaction",
          "turnId": "compaction",
          "content": "",
          "ts": "t4"
        },
        {
          "id": "session-terminated-t5",
          "role": "session_terminated",
          "turnId": "session-terminated",
          "content": "",
          "ts": "t5"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "in_turn_cards",
      "why": "Plan, todos, widget and question rows fold inside an open turn. The plan row deliberately carries no ts of its own.",
      "events": [
